{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The current best configuration is config_005 (RNA-only, scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.650 accuracy. The only multimodal test (config_030: same RNA branch + ResNet50, concat fusion) yielded 0.632, a slight degradation. This raises the question of whether the underperformance is due to the naive concat fusion mechanism (which forces equal-weight combination of a strong RNA signal and a weak image signal) or due to the inherently weak ResNet50 image features (0.208 alone). Config_031 changes only the fusion strategy from concat to weighted, holding all other variables identical to config_030 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, ResNet50). This single-variable comparison cleanly isolates the fusion effect: if weighted fusion recovers or exceeds 0.650, it confirms that the image signal is useful but was being diluted by unweighted concatenation, validating the multimodal direction; if it does not help, it strongly implicates the ResNet50 encoder as the bottleneck, justifying a shift to ViT-L in subsequent experiments. This is the most informative next step because it resolves a critical design ambiguity with minimal confounding, directly informing whether further multimodal budget should be spent on better fusion or better image encoders."
}

